# cavet engine release control. This file present at the tagged commit means
# the engine image content is unchanged since the version named below, and the
# release workflow retags that image instead of rebuilding it.
# Provenance-only edits (e.g. digest-pinning a base image that the previous
# build already used) do not change image content; a retag is still correct.
# Signatures carry over because cosign signs by digest: a retag preserves the
# manifest digest, so the signatures from the named release stay valid.
# DELETE this file in any PR that changes engine image content (Dockerfile,
# bundled scanners, entrypoint) so that release rebuilds and re-signs.
